Subject: Drop rocksdb -Werror so gcc 12 can compile compaction_picker_level.cc
Origin: DHI-internal
Description: rocksdb 7.8.3's CMakeLists appends -Werror after CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS,
 so a flag in bazel/rocksdb.BUILD cannot outrank it. gcc 12 turns a false
 positive in compaction_picker_level.cc into an error. patch_cmds rewrites
 that appended -Werror to -Wno-error=array-bounds before cmake runs.
Upstream tree: https://github.com/facebook/rocksdb/tree/v7.8.3

--- a/WORKSPACE
+++ b/WORKSPACE
@@ -209,6 +209,7 @@
     build_file = "//bazel:rocksdb.BUILD",
     remote = "https://github.com/facebook/rocksdb.git",
     tag = "v7.8.3",
+    patch_cmds = ["sed -i 's/ -Werror/ -Wno-error=array-bounds/' CMakeLists.txt"],
 )
 
 http_archive(
